      "writtenOn": "2022-07-05T10:34:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This cause an issue when testing Reconfiguration scenario (Media-\u003eConversational).\nThis is because stack remembers CIS_ID for devices which uses configuration caching. (I think we might need unittest for that).\n\nHere is patch which should give some lights on that: https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Bluetooth/+/2045727/\n\nAnyways, to make it work on my end I had to add here this:\n\n```\n   do {\n     /* CIS ID already set */\n     if (ase-\u003ecis_id !\u003d kInvalidCisId) {\n-      cises_[ase-\u003ecis_id].addr \u003d leAudioDevice-\u003eaddress_;\n-      LOG_DEBUG(\" ASE ID: %d, is already assigned CIS ID: %d\", +ase-\u003eid,\n-                +ase-\u003ecis_id);\n-      continue;\n+      LOG_DEBUG(\" ASE ID: %d, is already assigned CIS ID: %d, type %d\",\n+                +ase-\u003eid, +ase-\u003ecis_id, cises_[ase-\u003ecis_id].type);\n+        if (cises_[ase-\u003eid].addr !\u003d RawAddress::kEmpty) {\n+          LOG_DEBUG(\"Bidirectional ASE already assigned \");\n+          continue;\n+        }\n     }\n```",
      "revId": "92b9c991e07eb48836a124dd37c542392938cd6a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
